{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BWT11n272RF6w54kgRfdRx","type":"tool_result","content":"def format_term(term: Term) -> str:\n    \"\"\"`(('a', 1.0), ('b', 0.5), ('c', -1.0))` -> `a · sqrt(b) / c`.\"\"\"\n    def factor(name: str, e: float) -> str:\n        e = abs(e)\n        if e == 1.0:\n            return name\n        if e == 0.5:\n            return f\"sqrt({name})\"\n        if e == 2.0:\n            return f\"{name}²\"\n        return f\"{name}^{e:g}\"\n\n    num = [factor(f, e) for f, e in term if e > 0]\n    den = [factor(f, e) for f, e in term if e < 0]\n    text = \" · \".join(num) if num else \"1\"\n    if den:\n        text += \" / \" + (den[0] if len(den) == 1 else \"(\" + \" · \".join(den) + \")\")\n    return text\n\n\ndef enumerate_terms(columns: list[str], positive: set[str], max_degree: int = 3) -> list[Term]:\n    \"\"\"All monomials of at most `max_degree` distinct features with the\n    exponent sets of `EXPONENTS`; a negative exponent only on a column that\n    is strictly positive everywhere.\"\"\"\n    terms: list[Term] = []\n    for degree in range(1, max_degree + 1):\n        exps = EXPONENTS[degree]\n        for combo in itertools.combinations(columns, degree):\n            for es in itertools.product(exps, repeat=degree):\n                if any(e < 0 and f not in positive for f, e in zip(combo, es)):\n                    continue\n                terms.append(tuple(zip(combo, es)))\n    return terms\n\n\ndef evaluate_terms(values: dict[str, np.ndarray], terms: list[Term]) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Matrix of term values, one row per term.\"\"\"\n    n = len(next(iter(values.values())))\n    out = np.ones((len(terms), n), dtype=float)\n    for i, term in enumerate(terms):\n        for f, e in term:\n            out[i] *= values[f] ** e\n    return out\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the two-parameter fit, cross-validated, vectorised over terms\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n---- EXTREMAL\n99:def matrix_key(matrix: np.ndarray) -> str:\n104:def matrix_from_key(key: str) -> np.ndarray:\n108:def instance_from_matrix(matrix: np.ndarray, prefix: str = \"x\") -> MOSPInstance:\n113:def graph_certificate(matrix: np.ndarray) -> str:\n126:def lower_bounds(instance: MOSPInstance) -> dict:\n146:def evaluate(matrix: np.ndarray, solutions_dir: Path = SCRATCH_SOLUTIONS,\n196:def score(rec: dict, objective: str) -> tuple:\n206:def tree_of_cliques(n: int, rng: np.random.Generator, extra_columns: int = 2) -> np.ndarray:\n231:def bernoulli(n: int, rng: np.random.Generator) -> np.ndarray:\n241:def subset_of(matrix: np.ndarray, n: int, rng: np.random.Generator) -> np.ndarray:\n253:def mutate(matrix: np.ndarray, rng: np.random.Generator) -> np.ndarray:\n275:def gap_seed_matrices() -> list[np.ndarray]:\n295:def local_search(seed: np.ndarray, objective: str, steps: int, rng: np.random.Generator,\n346:def cur_matrix(rec: dict) -> np.ndarray:\n350:def kick(matrix: np.ndarray, rng: np.random.Generator, flips: int = 3) -> np.ndarray:\n358:def _search_job(args) -> dict:\n379:def search_jobs(objectives=OBJECTIVES, sizes=SEARCH_SIZES, extra_sizes=PWTW_EXTRA_SIZES,\n401:def run_search(workers: int, steps: int, restarts=(5, 3, 4), sizes=SEARCH_SIZES,\n439:def corpus_frame() -> pd.DataFrame:\n446:def _corpus_instances(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> list[tuple[pd.Series, MOSPInstance]]:\n453:def _tw_job(args) -> dict:\n496:def run_corpus(workers: int, max_n_all: int = 20, deadline: float = 60.0,\n528:def corpus_baselines(frame: pd.DataFrame, corpus_tw: pd.DataFrame | None,\n550:def best_per_cell(jobs: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n570:def recertify(key: str, solutions_dir: Path = SCRATCH_SOLUTIONS) -> dict:\n616:def draw(key: str, title: str) -> str:\n628:def core_key(key: str) -> str:\n644:def proof_block(key: str, solutions_dir: Path = SCRATCH_SOLUTIONS) -> tuple[dict, str]:\n680:def _md(