{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfSSTsPEZRXb785wPoZGX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qt6rbdYWrXeBYgiVkhTmBL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /tmp/it10 && cat > /tmp/it10/head.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 23. Conjecture mining: is there a branching-aware lower bound, and does it survive an adversary? (plan 2 §2.6, loop0003 item 09)\n\n*2026-09-26. Code: `learning/conjecture.py`. Regenerate:*\n\n```bash\npython -m learning.conjecture --stage invariants --workers 16   # every certified instance, ~25 min on 16 workers\npython -m learning.conjecture --stage mine                      # candidates, validity, hold-out, ranking (~3 min)\npython -m learning.conjecture --stage attack --workers 16       # 10,240 oracle evaluations per survivor\npython -m learning.conjecture --stage tables                    # reports/conjecture_tables.md\npython -m pytest tests/test_conjecture.py -q\n```\n\n*Writes `learning/data/ensemble/conjecture_invariants.csv.gz` (one row per\ncertified instance), `conjecture_candidates.csv` (one row per candidate),\n`conjecture_attack.csv` (one row per search job), `conjecture_counterexamples.csv`\nand `reports/conjecture_tables.md`. Generated witnesses go to the git-ignored\n`learning/data/conjecture/solutions/`; nothing is written to `solutions/`, and\nno candidate reaches `_lower_bound` or any path that decides `k`.*\n\n**Question.** §6 showed that three of the four components of the proved\nbound `lb_best` are lower bounds on treewidth and §21 that pathwidth strictly\nexceeds treewidth on at least 48.5% of the 338 corpus instances where `lb_best`\nmisses by two or more, so no degree or clique argument can be tight there.\nThe family the bound misses is *trees of cliques with branching*. Is there a\nformula over invariants that see branching which is never above the optimum on\nevery certified instance we have, exceeds `lb_best` on more than 5% of the\ngap instances, and survives an adversary that searches for a counterexample\nwith the exact solver as oracle?\n\n**Method.** (1) *Invariants*, all of the MOSP graph and recomputed from the\nmatrix for every certified instance — the corpus (6,376 at 9–134 customers),\nthe campaign (37,800 at 10–40) and the upward run (6,773 certified at\n50–100): exact treewidth by the subset DP at n ≤ 26 and by §21's decision\nsearch under a 1 s deadline at 27–64 (a censored call keeps its interval, and\n`tw_lo` is always a valid lower bound on treewidth; above 64, MMD and min-fill\nonly); the expansion profile `f(1..6)` of `satisfiability.expansion_bound`\nunder a 0.5 s budget, exact levels only, and the bound they prove; the\nclique number, exact; articulation points, blocks, bridges; the pathwidth of\nthe block–cut tree by the Ellis–Sudborough–Turner recursion (a vertex with\nthree branches of pathwidth ≥ k forces ≥ k + 1; tested against the exact DP\non random trees); the number of articulation points with three or more\nbranches; the **branch-lemma bound** `blt` — over every vertex whose removal\nleaves three or more components, the third-largest treewidth of a component\nplus one, a lower bound on pathwidth by the same lemma since pw(B) ≥ tw(B);\nsimplicial vertices; and the pathwidth of a deterministic clique tree of the\nMCS-M chordal completion (`ct_pw`, a computable quantity rather than a graph\ninvariant, labelled as such). Beside them the heuristics the feature table\nalready had (`tw_min_fill`, `bw_rcm`, `sep_size`), the degree statistics,\ndegeneracy and contraction degeneracy. (2) *Candidates*: every monomial of at\nmost two invariants from `learning.formula_search.enumerate_terms` (exponents\n±2, ±1, ±½), each turned into a bound three ways — *raw*, the integer term\nitself, whose `above` count is the check that a theorem is a theorem;\n*additive* `⌊t + b⌋` with `b` the largest constant that is valid on every\ncertified row; *scaled* `⌊a · t⌋` likewise. A constant fitted on every row is\nvalid by construction, so two honest checks follow: the constant re-chosen on\nfour fifths of the file ∪ isomorphism-class groups (`learning.fingerprint.union_groups`;\nthe campaign grouped by cell ∪ class) and applied to the fifth held out\n(`holdout_above`, the number of held-out rows the candidate then overshoots),\nand the adversary. (3) *Ranking*: `exceed`, the fraction of the 338 corpus\ngap ≥ 2 instances on which the candidate is strictly above `lb_best`;\n`tight`, where it equals the optimum; the mean shortfall. Candidates with the\nsame value vector on the 338 are one candidate, the simplest formula kept.\n(4) *The adversary*: every distinct survivor is attacked by `learning.extremal.local_search`\nwith the objective `f(G) − optimum`, `solve_mosp_exact` as oracle, at n = 8–15\nfrom tree-of-cliques and Bernoulli seeds, two restarts of 320 evaluations per\nsize and seed family: 10,240 oracle evaluations per candidate, canonical\nduplicates skipped. The smallest counterexample of each broken candidate is\nre-certified (exact solver, both refutation configurations at `optimum − 1`\nand `optimum`, the lattice oracle, the pathwidth DP) and drawn.\n\n**Baseline.** `lb_best` as the solver computes it, and the expansion bound\nalone (§6, the one pathwidth argument among the components).\n\n**Kill (plan 2 §2.6).** The family is closed if no candidate exceeds\n`lb_best` on more than 5% of the gap instances while surviving the adversary.\nEOF\ntail -1 /home/al/dev/MOSP/learning/data/ensemble/conjecture_run.log; date","description":"Draft static report text; check run progress"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2429,"cache_read_input_tokens":181857,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2429,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnost